   My advice here is that debating "rationality" and "irrationality"
   tends to be a semantic quibble. And discussing the concepts that are
   most often thought of as "irrational," such as reincarnation, ghosts,
   communication with the dead, astrology, faerie spirits, etc., is very
   much outside the set of topics people on this List are interested in
   talking about.

Incidentally, I have an interest in astrology from a (psychological?)
(semantic?) (marketing?) standpoint.  I wonder how people manage to
write stuff that looks specific in a general way, or general in a
specific way, or whatever, such that millions of people think it
refers to them.  Even more interesting I find why they think the other
eleven signs worth of stuff _doesn't_ refer to them.

